nd of gone until i want it back  on top of that my lower jaw can be  stretched up to six feet that's two  meters for those of you weirdos who use  the metric system in any direction so in  addition to being a juggler and a clown  i also made the killing as a geek at  herman fellas circus i don't mean geek  as in owned a signed james t kirk funko  pop that's still in mint condition i  mean the sense of somebody who gets paid  the weird junk as a form of performance  although i have been accused by some of  being both now you're probably thinking  motormouth my power my good body there's  so many careers you could have gone into  with that very specific set of skills  garbage disposal one-man moving band  service left luggage attendant at grand  central station sky's the limit man well  sure but i love the circus they're the  only family i've ever got in this world  that came to them when i was just a why  that punk kid of eight years old and  they took me in like i was their own  flesh and blood yeah believe it or not i  wasn't actually born into the circus  life a lot of circus and performing arts  folks are born into the industry born in  a costume trunk as they say but  unfortunately that's not me i was born  in new york city on april 10th 1976. my  dad had took off long before i showed up  leaving me in the care of my dear old  mom my special abilities manifested  early and my mom recognized them right  away you know how little kids are always  putting things in their mouths right  it's cute when it's a block or an action  figure but less so when it's the entire  coffee table yeah my mom was fully aware  of what i could do and she hated my guts  for it not only had a baby daddy flown  the coop but the kid she was racing was  a freak of nature who she could barely  stand to look at and trust me the  feelings of resentment were totally  mutual one of my favorite pastimes as a  youngster was to go out and find as many  small animals as i could get my little  hands on then go back inside where mom  was laid out on the pilot chair sleeping  off one of her special grown-up  headaches she got from downing a bottle  and a half of a special grown-up juice i  made like i was going to innocently ask  her a question smiling one of those  adorable little eight-year-old smiles  then instead of saying anything i just  barf up a couple dozen rats onto her lap  despite how much i hated living at home  it never occurred to me that i could  leave i was a pretty wide-eyed kid monk  kept me isolated from the wider world i  guess had a fear that i'd eat somebody  but one night as i was going to bed i  met manny who's manny  come on if you know anything about the  circus of disquieting then you know  manny don't you guys already have a  video on that manny's short for the man  with the upside down face he was herman  fuller's right hand in charge of a lot  of the backstage stuff including shall  we say  talent acquisition who knows how he  figured out where i was or that i could  even do what i do but just like magic he  showed up in my window should i have  been worried that a man with an upside  down face was at my window probably but  i guess i was just happy to see someone  who was more of a freak than me manny  offered me a place in a real family  where i wouldn't be cooped up he said  that freaks belonged out in the world  sharing their talents making people  laugh and cry and puke all over the  place i didn't hesitate i took him up on  this offer mommy dearest was so deep in  the drink that she didn't even notice i  left and that was that from that day  forward i was a member of hermann  fuller's family i never looked back not  even once now it may also surprise you  to know that i wasn't always the picture  of confidence i am today my first job  with the circus was as the human clown  car as a kid i didn't have a lot of  stage presence and i didn't talk much so  the natural thing to do was to send me  out to the ring and let the clown  through come mouching out of my mouth to  the surprise and delight of the audience  i learned juggling from a guy named  scythe he was a human pin cushion but  like most of us at hermann fuller his  abilities were way beyond what you'd see  in any common or gotham circus scythe  was incredible at what he did you could  stick a shiv in every square inch of  this guy and he'd never bat an eye  thorough jerk though and awful with kids  so how he got the job of training me in  the ways of the juggler is totally  beyond me if i so much as talked out of  turn he'd beam me in the head with a  juggling pin not hard just enough to  hurt i know that sounds bad but at least  it toughened me up i think scythe was  jealous of me in hindsight i was  unnatural and i think he saw me as you  know some kind of threat scythe  eventually died and the fire stunt gone  wrong i owed a funeral for him but i was  busy that day clowning i learned from a  guy called scruffy mcgrubbins good old  scruffy he had all the grace and  countenance of a chain smoking grizzly  bear and he was worth more than all the  grandmothers i never had he never talked  to me like i was stupid the way most  people talk to kids scruffy took me  seriously and he embodied unto me all  the knowledge he'd picked up in his  years in the circus trade he was a very  wise man as clowns go he never mince  words never messed around with small  talk he just jumped straight into a  conversation and expected you to catch  up i never knew what happened to the guy  i already quit the clown biz and settled  down in a nice apartment in kent i hope  he's having a good day wherever he is so  i did the juggling thing for a while  bossing around balls and bins and other  junk and catching it in my mouth  sometimes i'd put a plant in the  audience call them up and swallow them  whole as a part of the act eventually i  started working on a double act with  another freak by the name of theo see  theo could flip himself inside out but  he was also pretty skilled acrobat so  he'd do a high dive jump over the  audience before his insides outside then  aim himself down my gullet he was a  pretty great act if i do say so myself  and i even dated for a while what can i  say i find guys just as fun to swallow  as gals after he and i broke it off i  decided i needed to change up my act  that's when it hit me motormouth picture  this here's me an assistant on either  side ready to pull my mouth open then a  chrysler comes barreling into a big top  hits a ramp drives right into my mouth  into my second stomach it was a  dangerous act a magic shirt but not  immune to being run over but it was the  best act i ever came up with i could  tell you some stories about my time with  the circus oh there was this one time my  tapeworm started talking to me at the  time i was involved in overthrowing  roman follower himself and installing  ikky as a new ringmaster at the time i  hooked up with one of the non-human  capital c clowns so this is a  family-friendly channel so maybe not  that one that's not what you want to  hear though is it you'd rather hear  about how i got myself captured and  locked up by the miss scp foundation  all right why not i've already spilled  the rest of my backstory so manny you  remember manny from earlier right he  saved a lot of kids like me and when he  did he usually put me in charge of  teaching them how to perform but there  was this one girl he brought in who  broke down crying in the middle of one  of our juggling lessons she said she  wanted to go home that's when i knew  that manny had graduated from saving  runaways and abused kids like me to  abducting kids with powers of course i  confronted him about it i told him point  blank that's not how we do things  anymore herman hadn't been around for  years at this point we were better than  that gave me some garbage about him  doing what he had to do to keep the  circus alive  can you believe that even with  everything we were doing he 